# Copy to .env and fill in. `pnpm dev:autoplay` loads it via dotenv-cli.
# Every key is optional at boot — the app renders an OFF AIR screen listing
# whatever is missing instead of crashing. All keys are needed for the full
# station: sign-in → the lineup → the stream → the replay.

# X (Twitter) OAuth 2.0 app — https://console.x.com
# These are the OAuth 2.0 Client ID / Client Secret, NOT the OAuth 1.0a
# Consumer Key / Secret Key / Bearer Token shown when the app is created.
# Create the app, then enable "User authentication settings":
#   Type of app:  Web App (confidential client)
#   Callback URIs: http://127.0.0.1:3005/api/auth/callback/twitter
#                  https://autoplay.kyh.io/api/auth/callback/twitter
#   X rejects "localhost" in a callback — use 127.0.0.1 and set APP_URL to
#   match, then browse http://127.0.0.1:3005 rather than localhost.
#   Scopes used:  tweet.read users.read offline.access
# The provider sets disableDefaultScope (src/lib/auth.ts) — better-auth would
# otherwise append users.email, which X grants only to apps approved for it.
# The X API is pay-per-use since Feb 2026 — there is no free tier, and a new
# account with a $0 balance gets 402 on the first call. Buy credits and set a
# spending cap at console.x.com first. Home timeline reads cost $0.005 per
# post returned, so one 50-post page is ~$0.25; the owner's own posts
# (`/2/users/:id/tweets`) are $0.001 per post.
X_CLIENT_ID=""
X_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# The X handle whose feed powers the default public channel (CH 01). It is
# live only while this account is signed in and watching; everyone else
# watches the replay of what it recorded.
OWNER_X_USERNAME=""

# better-auth signing secret (sign-in with X). Sessions and the X tokens
# live in the Turso database, so sign-in also needs TURSO_DATABASE_URL.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=""

# fal.ai — https://fal.ai/dashboard/keys
# Every channel streams through the H3 Max Director model, billed per second
# of session ($0.08/s list, 60s minimum per session). The browser reaches fal
# through /api/fal/proxy, which holds this key; src/lib/live.ts caps the day.
FAL_KEY=""

# autoplay's OWN Turso database (do not reuse policingice's): users, sessions,
# grants, the lineup, and what has aired. Create one with
# `turso db create autoplay`, then push the schema once:
#   pnpm -F @repo/autoplay db:push
# Unlike policingice, db:push here is safe — this database belongs to this
# app alone. Without these keys aired items live in server memory only, and
# sign-in (which needs somewhere to store users) is unavailable.
TURSO_DATABASE_URL="libsql://<database>-<org>.turso.io"
TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN=""

# Optional. Vercel Blob store for the public channel's recordings, which are
# the replay everyone but the owner watches. Connect a store to the project
# (`vercel blob create-store autoplay --access public`, then link it) and this
# lands in the environment on its own; pull it locally with `vercel env pull`.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""

# Optional. Public origin used for the OAuth redirect URI when deployed
# behind a proxy; defaults to the request origin (fine for localhost).
APP_URL=""

# Optional. Google OAuth app, for the Gmail (newsletters) and YouTube sources
# — https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/credentials. Web application type;
# authorized redirect URIs:
#   http://127.0.0.1:3005/api/auth/callback/google
#   https://autoplay.kyh.io/api/auth/callback/google
# Enable the Gmail API and the YouTube Data API v3 on the project. Scopes are
# requested when a source is connected (gmail.readonly, youtube.readonly);
# gmail.readonly is a restricted scope, so an app open to the public needs
# Google's verification — a personal deploy can stay in Testing mode with the
# owner as a test user. Google is never a way to sign in: it is linked to the
# X-signed-in user.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=""
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=""

# Sign-up is invite only: a new viewer gives a code before signing in with X,
# and an account is created only if the code has a use left. Codes live in
# the database, minted from the shell — see scripts/create-invite.ts:
#   pnpm -F @repo/autoplay invite --code VICKIE --max-uses unlimited
#   pnpm -F @repo/autoplay invite --list
